INT. GRAND PLAZA HOTEL, BALLROOM B - ARBITRATION HEARING - DAY

A long table with water pitchers and legal pads. A banner for a dental convention is still hanging on the wall. Five people sit with their binders open.

                    HARGREAVE
          Ms. Ottoline, for the record, your client signed the second addendum on the fourteenth.

                    OTTOLINE
          My client signed a draft on the fourteenth. A draft is not an addendum.

                    RAFFERTY
          It had a signature page.

                    OTTOLINE
          It had a signature line, Mr. Rafferty. There's a distinction.

                    SUNITA
          Arbitrator, may I interject?

                    HARGREAVE
          You may, Ms. Desai.

                    SUNITA
          The addendum was circulated by email, acknowledged by email, and acted on within forty-eight hours. Whatever Ms. Ottoline calls it, her client behaved as if it were binding.

                    OTTOLINE
          Behaved. Not agreed.

                    LORCAN
          If I may, Arbitrator. The payments began on the sixteenth.

                    OTTOLINE
          Mr. Lorcan, with respect, you are a witness, not counsel.

                    LORCAN
          I'm both. It's a small firm.

                    HARGREAVE
          Order, please.

                    RAFFERTY
          Arbitrator, the payments are the point. Our client sent fifteen thousand dollars each month for six months.

                    OTTOLINE
          Under protest.

                    SUNITA
          Under what protest? There's no letter.

                    OTTOLINE
          There's a voicemail.

                    RAFFERTY
          A voicemail.

                    OTTOLINE
          Time-stamped and transcribed.

                    HARGREAVE
          Is the transcript in evidence?

                    OTTOLINE
          Exhibit nine.

                    LORCAN
          Exhibit nine is blank.

                    OTTOLINE
          It is not blank, it is redacted.

                    SUNITA
          Redacted by whom?

                    OTTOLINE
          By the court reporter.

                    HARGREAVE
          Ms. Ottoline, the court reporter works for me.

                    OTTOLINE
          Then I suspect she followed instructions.

                    HARGREAVE
          Mine?

                    OTTOLINE
          I didn't say yours.

Nobody speaks. The banner behind them sags a little on its tape. A dental hygienist pokes her head through the door, takes one look at the room, and withdraws.
